WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.267
-Hey, everybody, welcome back
to the show.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:05.300
Just a reminder, we have
a new thing we're doing

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.701
called the Fallon Book Club.

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:07.934
We're starting a book club.

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:09.601
Yesterday, we announced
our very first book --

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:13.667
"Tomorrow and Tomorrow and
Tomorrow" by Gabrielle Zevin.

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:15.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:18.100
I'm gonna be reading this
over the next few weeks.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.334
I started reading it
a little bit.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:21.334
-When, last night?
-No, this is --

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.801
like, a couple weeks ago.
I did a little research.

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:25.534
I had to start a little bit,
just so I know what book

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:27.267
I want to choose
for the book club,

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:28.601
but this is the one.
This is the jam.

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:30.467
It's a love story-ish.

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:33.067
Well, it's like --
it's set in the '90s.

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:35.267
These two kids haven't seen
each other in a while.

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:37.133
They know each other
from school.

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.601
They're computer nerds.

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:41.367
They start a video game
together.

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:43.234
They create a video game
together,

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:45.334
and then you see what happens.

00:00:45.334 --> 00:00:47.100
-Mm-hmm.
-Yeah.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.000
You know what I liked about it,
though, is the line in here --

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.234
he sees this girl he hasn't seen
since grade school or something

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:54.601
or high school,
and he sees her on the train

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:55.534
and he yells out her name.

00:00:55.534 --> 00:00:56.834
He's like, "Sadie Green,"

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:58.601
and she doesn't turn around.
He's like, "Sadie Green."

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:01.734
He goes, "Sadie Green,
you died of dysentery."

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.033
And she turns around
'cause if anyone --

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:04.801
Do you remember that game --
"Oregon Trail"?

00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:06.934
-Oh, yeah.
-So it's like a good --

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:08.167
it's a really funny line.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.634
I go, "Oh, that's
a good reference."

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:12.000
So anyways, so it's like that.
It's well-written. It's good.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.033
If you want to follow along
with me,

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:16.334
pick up a copy,
go to your local library.

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:18.300
I will be posting updates
on my socials

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.167
to let you know where I'm at
and what I think of the book.

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:22.501
Then later, we'll have
the author, Gabrielle Zevin,

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.000
on the show to talk about it.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.534
It is the Fallon Book Club.
-Oh!

00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:27.100
-It is gonna be fun.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.801
FBC! FBC!

